              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">e95d95e7-5ac6-5f8c-bd5f-77ba9fa493f0</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: Where exhaled CO2 goes around a breathing person in a small room.
Fidelity: Engineering - transient CFD around a simplified manikin, not validated.
Method: Indoor Species Case solves CO2 as mass (OpenFOAM multicomponentFluid): 12 breaths a minute at 40000 ppm for 10 s.
Result: CO2 traces 0.15 m ahead of the mouth and in the far corner; the near one swings from about 20000 ppm to ambient each breath.
Needs: Eddy3D Setup &gt; Fully-coupled multi-region CFD / HAM / RAD / VEG (urbanMicroclimateFoam); multicomponentFluid ships only in the UMF image. Runtime: minutes.
Edit: Manikin position and facing, breathing rate, room size, vent position.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
